---
description: Scan selected digital books before content use and record hash-bound security evidence
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the book-security policy in `AGENTS.md` and `docs/BOOK_SECURITY.md`.
When a digital book is downloaded or selected for reading, parsing, conversion,
or filing, run `python3 tools/book_security.py /absolute/path/to/book.pdf`.
The helper reuses only a current successful scan for matching bytes, engine,
signature databases and policy, and updates known digital catalog holdings.
Results and raw logs remain in ignored `.local/`.
An absent scanner, stale definitions, error, encryption, or exceeded limit is a
hold, never a successful scan. Do not process a held book or automatically move,
delete, quarantine, upload, or execute it. Scan derived reading copies too.
This is an agent workflow gate, not a background watcher or OS-wide on-access scan.
